cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "autoMIL: Autonomous Agent-Driven Multiple Instance Learning for Computational Pathology"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shuolin
    family-names: Yin
    email: leo.yin@mail.utoronto.ca
  - given-names: Yeonwoo
    family-names: Seo
  - given-names: Jun
    family-names: Ma
    # corresponding author
repository-code: "https://github.com/leoyin1127/autoMIL"
url: "https://automil.org"
abstract: >-
  autoMIL is an autonomous experiment framework for Multiple Instance Learning
  in computational pathology. It overlays onto existing ML project repositories,
  enabling coding agents to iteratively improve models through persistent
  experimentation, knowledge accumulation, and multi-branch exploration.
keywords:
  - multiple-instance-learning
  - computational-pathology
  - whole-slide-imaging
  - automl
  - autonomous-agents
  - experiment-tracking
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
